  "raw_text": "317\n\nVERB TO NOUN #3 /\n \nDE\n \nVERBO\n \nA\n \nSUSTANTIVO #3\n \n–\n\nINSTRUMENT FORM / FORMA INSTRUMENTO\n\nBy adding “\naika\n” to\n \nthe root of the verb, the instrument form is formed. This form refers to something that does the\naction of the verb. /\n\nAl agregar \"\naika\n\" a la raíz del verbo, se forma\n \nla forma\n \ninstrumento. Esta forma se refiere a algo que hace la acción del\n\nverbo.\n\nExamples/Ejemplos:\n\nVerb/Verbo\n \nRoot/Raíz\n \n+\n \naika\n \n→\n \nInstrument Form / Forma Instrumento\n\nAiklabaia\n \n–\n \nto fight\n \n/ luchar\n \nAiklab\n \n+\n \naika\n \n→\n \nAiklabaika\n \n–\n \nweapon\n \n/ arma\n\nAuhbaia\n \n–\n \nto fill, to store\n \n/\n\nllenar, almacenar\n\nAuhb\n \n+\n \naika\n \n→\n \nAuhbaika\n \n–\n \nsomething used to store\n \nthings, a\n\ncontainer\n \n/ algo usado para\n \nalmacenar cosas, un\n\ncontenedor\n\nBapaia\n \n–\n \nto stand something\n\nup\n \n/ levantar algo\n\nBap\n \n+\n \naika\n \n→\n \nBapaika\n \n–\n \na stand\n \n/ pie (de sost\né\nn), atril,\n \nperchero\n\nDimaia\n \n–\n \nto enter\n \n/ entrar\n \nDim\n \n+\n \naika\n \n→\n \nDimaika\n \n–\n \nentrance, entryway, gate\n \n/ entrada,\n\npuerta\n\nTawan\nka dimaia\n \n–\n \nto enter\n\ntown\n \n/ entrar a la ciudad\n\nDim\n \n+\n \naika\n \n→\n \nTawanka dimaika\n \n–\n \ntown entrance, city\n \nentrance\n \n/\n\nentrada de la\n \nciudad\n\nIska krahbaia\n \n–\n \nto urinate\n \n/\n\nOrinar\n\nKrahb\n \n+\n \naika\n \n→\n \nIska krahbaika\n \n–\n \nurinal\n \n/ urinario\n\nIwaia\n \n–\n \nto reside, to dwell, to\n\nlive, to sit down\n \n/ residir,\n\nvivir, morar, habitar, sentarse\n\nIw\n \n+\n \naika\n \n→\n \nIwaika\n \n–\n \nchair, residence, place, position,\n \nseat\n \n/\n\nsilla, residencia, lugar, posición,\n \nasiento\n\nKahbaia\n \n–\n \nto put, to set\n \n/\n\nponer, fijar\n\nKahb\n \n+\n \naika\n \n→\n \nKahbaika\n \n–\n \nplace to put things\n \n/ lugar para poner\n\ncosas\n\nKaina kahbaia\n \n–\n \nto shield, to\n\nprotect\n \n/ defender, proteger\n\nKahb\n \n+\n \naika\n \n→\n \nKaina kahbaika\n \n–\n \nshield, something used to\n\nprotect\n \n/ escudo, algo usado para\n \nproteger\n\nMiusik kangbaia\n \n–\n \nto play a\n\nmusical instrument\n \n/ tocar un\n\ninstrumento musical\n\nKangb\n \n+\n \naika\n \n→\n \nMiusik kangbaika\n \n–\n \nmusical instrument\n \n/\n\ninstrumento musical\n\nPahbaia\n \n–\n \nto sweep\n \n/ barrer\n \nPahb\n \n+\n \naika\n \n→\n \nPahbaika\n \n–\n \nbroom\n \n/ escoba\n\nPruaia\n \n–\n \nto die\n \n/ morir\n \nPru\n \n+\n \naika\n \n→\n \nPruaika\n \n–\n \nsomething that causes death\n \n/\n \nalgo que\n\ncausa la muerte\n\nPulaia\n \n–\n \nto play\n \n/ jugar\n \nPul\n \n+\n \naika\n \n→\n \nPulaika\n \n–\n \ntoy\n \n/ j\nuguete\n\nPura bikaia\n \n–\n \nto cover\n \n/ cubrir\n \nBik\n \n+\n \naika\n \n→\n \nPura bikaika\n \n–\n \ncovering, lid\n \n/ cubriendo, tapa\n\nTasba tukbaia\n \n–\n \nto hoe, to\n\nplow\n \n/ azotar, arar\n\nTukb\n \n+\n \naika\n \n→\n \nTasba tukbaika\n \n–\n \nhoe, plow / azada,\n\narado\n\nTwilkaia\n \n–\n \nto carry on the\n\nback, to hold up, to support,\n\nto carry\n \n/ llevar sobre la\n\nespalda, sostener\n\nTwilk\n \n+\n \naika\n \n→\n \nTwilkaika\n \n–\n \nsomething used to carrying on the\n\nback, yoke, something used to support, something\n\nused to carry\n \n/ algo que solía llevar en la espalda,\n\nyugo, algo que solía soportar, algo que solía llevar\n\nYukuwaia\n \n–\n \nto be hidden, to\n\nbe sheltered\n \n/ estar oculto,\n\nestar protegido\n\nYukuw\n \n+\n \naika\n \n→\n \nYukuwaika\n \n–\n \nhiding place\n \n/\n \nescondite",
